.IR Y ,
65 bytes); scalars and coordinates are 32-byte big-endian.
.PP
.B Ecdsa_verify
checks an ECDSA-with-SHA-256 signature:
.I hash
is the 32-byte digest,
.I r
and
.I s
the signature integers, and
.I pub
the signer's 65-byte public point. It returns 1 only if the signature
is valid and the public key is a well-formed on-curve point.
.B Ecdh_new
generates an ephemeral keypair, returning the 32-byte private scalar
and the 65-byte public point.
.B Ecdh_shared
computes the shared secret from our private scalar and the peer's
public point \(em the 32-byte big-endian
.I x
